1. Window mismatch / stale range — NOT REPRODUCED.
   - Enumerated every page-data shape via full-repo grep for `"StartDate"` in
     internal/handlers/*.go: it is set in EXACTLY 4 files (dashboard, explorer,
     insights, majorexpenses handlers.go), each a map[string]interface{} built
     from that page's OWN resolved start/end (already used elsewhere on the
     same page for date-input values / hx-get URLs, e.g. dashboard.html:51-52,
     explorer.html:78-79, insights.html:17-18/317, major-expenses.html:19-20).
     withRange reads that same field, so the nav link cannot diverge from what
     the page is already displaying — verified by rendering the real base.html
     via the embedded FS with StartDate=2025-06-30/EndDate=2025-01-01
     (start>end): propagated verbatim into both hrefs, matching "propagate
     current window as-is" (not "validate it") — go test -run TestZZZ_StartAfterEnd PASS.
   - Round-trip: each of the 4 handlers parses `?start=`/`?end=` with
     time.Parse("2006-01-02", ...) and formats back with the identical layout,
     so Dashboard->Explorer via a propagated link reproduces Explorer's own
     StartDate/EndDate bit-identical to the URL it was given; Explorer then
     re-propagates its OWN (not Dashboard's) resolved value on its own nav,
     confirmed by reading explorer/handlers.go:223-224 writing into the same
     map key withRange reads.
   - Lone `start` (no `end`): dashboard/insights/majorexpenses's resolveDateRange-
     style logic always fills the missing side with a default (YTD start or
     MaxDate) BEFORE writing StartDate/EndDate into the map — so the map field
     is always either both-populated (mirroring the page's real, fully-resolved
     window) or both-absent; a genuine half-window key pair into extractDateRange
     never occurs from a real handler. Confirmed via existing worker test
     TestBaseNav_EmptyRangeStringsRenderBareLinks (empty-string case) and
     TestWithRange_Unit's "map with empty-string dates" case — both bare, no
     `?start=&end=`.
   - Dates outside data's min/max, or unparseable start (malformed -> zero
     time.Time): pre-existing dashboard/insights parsing behavior untouched by
     this diff (resolveDateRange predates U8, only majorexpenses handlers.go
     was touched by U8's manifest and that touch was in parseRangeFromRequest's
     unrelated fallback path, not the date-parse logic) — and even so, the
     nav link mirrors the SAME bad value already shown in the page's own date
     inputs, so it is not a NEW mismatch introduced by U8. Out of task scope.

2. Injection / unsafe href — NOT REPRODUCED.
   withRange builds the query via url.Values{}.Encode() (percent-encodes),
   and the href attribute itself goes through html/template contextual
   auto-escaping on top. Probed via the real render pipeline
   (go test ./internal/templates/... -run TestZZZ_XSSInjectionViaStartDate,
   PASS) with 6 payloads: `"><script>alert(1)</script>`, `" onmouseover=`,
   `&evil=1`, `#frag`, embedded space, and Japanese unicode — no raw
   `<script>` tag, no attribute breakout, no verbatim unescaped payload in
   any href. (Note: in the real handlers this path can't even be reached
   with attacker strings, since StartDate/EndDate are always
   time.Parse+Format("2006-01-02") round-tripped before being written to
   the map — malformed input collapses to a canonical/zero date string, not
   passed through raw. Tested withRange directly regardless, per instructions.)

