OBSERVATIONS (not FAIL grounds — pre-existing, outside U8's manifest/contract):
- Page-local drilldown links from insights/major-expenses/alerts into
  /explorer?search=...&type=Outflow do not carry the current date range, so a
  user drilling into a specific transaction from a filtered window lands in
  Explorer's default (often YTD) window rather than the window they were
  looking at. This predates U8 and is out of its §2c scope (nav-only).
- Dashboard/insights's resolveDateRange-family functions silently produce a
  zero-value (0001-01-01) window on an unparseable `start`/`end` query param;
  pre-existing, unaffected by this diff, and consistent between display and
  nav propagation so it is not a mismatch this task introduces.
